; Typed literal characters as their glyphs (change ted-latin1-glyphs,
; spec editor/literal-characters "Display, help and colour"): blitz2 with
; a file of one empty line, type a string with an umlaut, a sharp s, a
; section sign and a degree sign (German keymap); the screen while the
; line is edited (getline draws each character as it is typed: printlit),
; then after Return (the line tokenised and drawn again: showa2item), with
; the cursor in the next row.  SAVE: the file holds the pairs.  TED-C
; only: the original TED cannot type these characters (@combos; 31-literal
; compares the two).
; @file typed.bas "\n"
; @source F typed.bas
; @combos C5 Cc
; @expect exists typed.bas
; @expect file typed.bas "Gr\x1b\x90\xdfe \x90\xa7\x90\xb0"
; @expect screen typing "  0 |a$=\"Gr\xc3\xb6\xc3\x9fe \xc2\xa7\xc2\xb0\""
; @expect screen typed "  0 |a$=\"Gr\xc3\xb6\xc3\x9fe \xc2\xa7\xc2\xb0\""
; @est 5
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
type "a$=\"Gr\xf6\xdfe \xa7\xb0\""
dump typing
type "\n"
dump typed
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
